+
+## Linked Comma 3X (FunnyPilot 3.7.3e source)
+
+This source adds **Linked hardware**, separate from browser sign-ins. It is not
+activated merely by editing the source: Worker deployment, broker activation and
+device installation/pairing are separate owner-authorized steps.
+
+A small Comma client polls outbound over HTTPS. It gets its own revocable token,
+never the host bridge secret. Selecting hardware starts a native Astra session at
+`/home/astro/Development/c3x`, with scoped MCP file/log/identity tools. Binding is
+immutable across resume; ambiguous native continue/picker/fork launches require an
+explicit `--resume UUID`. No provider/model or global harness settings change.
+
+Generic device commands require the **exact-command approval buttons**, fresh
+ignition-off state, and a short execution lease. Native terminal menus and bypass
+mode do not approve them. Unconfirmed commands are not replayed. Approved programs
+are privileged maintenance, not a sandbox. A current branch/commit match does not
+identify an older recording's code; the comparison tool reports that distinction.
+
+Run the complete local, no-model fixture suite with Node 24:
+
+```sh
+node scripts/test-device-link.mjs
+```
+
+It creates temporary Worker storage, synthetic credentials and build output; it
+never reads live `.dev.vars` or overwrites `dist`. For the Python integration,
+`ASTRA_TEST_PYTHON` defaults to `/tmp/fp-audit-venv/bin/python`, and the fixture
+imports the local c3x checkout. Details, protocol, activation caveats and the
+source patch are in `/home/astro/Development/c3x/docs/astra-link-3.7.3e.md`.

